# E2E tests (olie-e2e)

Management UI regressions that need a real browser belong in the sibling repo
**`../olie-e2e`** (Playwright), not inside this monorepo. Agents working on
`@olie/management` (and related UI) **can and should** add or update E2E specs
there when the change is user-visible.

## Stack

One compose brings API, fronts, and the e2e runner:

```bash
cd ../docker-workspace && docker compose up -d
```

`olie-e2e` stays up (`sleep infinity`). Dockerfile mirror:
`../docker-workspace/e2e/Dockerfile` (sync with `../olie-e2e/Dockerfile`).

## Run tests

```bash
cd ../docker-workspace
docker compose exec e2e npx playwright test --project=chromium
docker compose exec e2e npx playwright test --project=chromium tests/auth.smoke.spec.ts

# or:
cd ../olie-e2e && ./run.sh
```

Defaults: `tester@olie.ai` / `password` (api-main seed). Reports land in
`../olie-e2e/test-results` and `../olie-e2e/playwright-report`.

## Create / update specs

- Put files under `../olie-e2e/tests/` (feature gates: `tests/features/`).
- Reuse helpers: `tests/helpers/auth.ts`, `project.ts`, `content-media.ts`,
  `feature.ts` (`requireFeature` / `requireVisible` / `requireLogsFilterHidesMessage`).
- Prefer new projects via `createE2EProject` over hard-coded IDs.
- If the UI is missing on the branch under test, **skip** with `requireFeature`
  instead of failing.
- Do not commit secrets; optional overrides in `../olie-e2e/.env` (see `.env.example`).

## When to add an E2E

Add or extend a spec when changing user-visible flows in management (auth,
project details, Content widget / media filters, feature-flagged actions, etc.).
Unit/component tests stay in this repo; cross-app browser flows go to `olie-e2e`.
